Seemless WP7.5: VK_EXT_robustness2 robustBufferAccess2 and nullDescriptor
on Apple GPUs (S8 H3, H4), MoltenVK v1.4.2.

H3: report robustBufferAccess2 on Apple GPUs. MoltenVK already relies on
    Apple GPUs bounds-checking buffer accesses for robustBufferAccess. Known
    deviation: the bound is the Metal buffer binding's end, not the exact
    descriptor range. Size alignments report the spec maxima (4 / 256).
H4: report nullDescriptor. Null buffer descriptors (argument buffers both
    modes, CPU-side buffer descriptors, vertex buffers) point at one
    zero-filled, resident 64 KiB MTLBuffer instead of address 0. Null
    textures stay nil, which Apple GPUs read as zero. Known deviations:
    writes through a null UAV land in the shared zero buffer; a null vertex
    buffer reads (0,0,0,0), not (0,0,0,1).
Both need a residency set (macOS 15+).
